{"id":"n4-041","title":"Verb てくれませんか (〜te kuremasen ka)","jlptLevel":4,"shortExplanation":"A polite way to request someone to do something for you; 'Could you please', 'Would you please', 'Won't you'.","longExplanation":"The ～てくれませんか grammar point is used to ask someone politely to do something for you. It is formed by using the て-form of a verb followed by くれませんか. It translates to 'Could you please', 'Would you please', or 'Won't you' in English.","formation":"Verb-て form + くれませんか","examples":[{"jp":"ドアを開けてくれませんか。","romaji":"Doa wo akete kuremasen ka.","en":"Could you please open the door?","words":[{"surface":"ドア","vocabId":null},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"開け","vocabId":"1202450","reading":"あける","baseForm":"開ける"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"くれ","vocabId":"1514950","reading":"くれ","baseForm":"くれる"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5,6,7]},{"jp":"これを見てくれませんか。","romaji":"Kore wo mite kuremasen ka.","en":"Would you please take a look at this?","words":[{"surface":"これ","vocabId":"1628530","reading":"これ"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"見","vocabId":"1259290","reading":"みる","baseForm":"見る"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"くれ","vocabId":"1514950","reading":"くれ","baseForm":"くれる"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4,5,6,7]},{"jp":"手伝ってくれませんか。","romaji":"Tetsudatte kuremasen ka.","en":"Won't you help me?","words":[{"surface":"手伝っ","vocabId":"1328190","reading":"てつだう","baseForm":"手伝う"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"くれ","vocabId":"1514950","reading":"くれ","baseForm":"くれる"},{"surface":"ませ","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"ます"},{"surface":"ん","vocabId":null},{"surface":"か","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2,3,4,5]},{"jp":"明日、迎